{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFour Python command-test modules contain 22 audited prose blocks with incident history, duplicated mechanism explanation, or ornamental section banners. Scope was revalidated against `origin/main@50716c9aed87479e4347a4daf084c9778c8793f7`. Two old line ranges each contained two independent blocks; the stable IDs below enumerate them separately.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only the 22 allowlisted true leading docstrings and contiguous full-line comment blocks. Capture immutable before/final blobs and parse both with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. On comparison copies, remove only allowlisted leading `Expr(Constant(str))` nodes from `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, and `AsyncFunctionDef`; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require normalized AST equality.\n\nTokenize comments by enclosing symbol plus the next unchanged executable anchor. Reject changes to every inline comment, directive, and non-allowlisted full-line block. Runtime strings, regexes, marker text, imports, decorators, annotations, subprocess arguments, assertions, and test data remain byte/AST exact. Adjacent blank-line normalization is allowed only around an edited block.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `tests/unit/commands/test_close_disposition.py` — 1 block:\n  - `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/commands/test_compact_plan.py` — 8 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def store`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_fold_and_rebuild_cite_the_same_source_set`\n  - `D:test_neither_engine_cites_a_consumed_prior_snapshot`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_a_rebuild_ignores_a_stray_non_event_file`\n  - `D:test_a_rebuild_ignores_a_stray_non_event_file`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_the_snapshot_envelope_and_rename_back_appear_only_in_compact_plan`\n  - `D:test_the_snapshot_envelope_and_rename_back_appear_only_in_compact_plan`\n- `tests/unit/commands/test_lifecycle_cascade.py` — 5 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_an_eligible_parent_is_advanced_before_the_child`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_a_multi_level_chain_cascades_all_the_way_up`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def _cascading_edges`\n  - `D:test_claim_cascades_only_the_open_edge_and_says_so`\n- `tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py` — 8 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_the_walker_finds_a_live_outbound_duplicates_target`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_recorded_mode_returns_a_dead_target_that_live_mode_rejects`\n  - `D:test_the_three_seams_keep_their_names_and_signatures`\n  - `C:<module>:before:_SRC`\n  - `D:_replacement_walk_offenders`\n  - `D:test_the_replacement_link_walk_has_exactly_one_body`\n  - `D:test_the_owner_module_carries_the_reasoned_escape_marker`\n\n`D:<symbol>` is a true leading docstring. `C:<scope>:before:<code>` is the maximal contiguous full-line comment block immediately before that unchanged code anchor. No other comment/docstring is editable.\n\n## Preserved contracts and consumers\n- Close dispositions retain live-replacement-before-reason precedence, the reason-required classes, write-side refusal, completion-verifier bypass for valid administrative dispositions, and signed-manifest behavior.\n- Compaction retains fold/rebuild source-set and envelope parity, exclusion of consumed snapshots, non-event filtering, restore/data-loss guards, and construct-uniqueness enforcement.\n- Lifecycle cascade retains parent-first recursion, benign-race recheck and error identity, table-driven edge coverage, and `claim`'s sole supported `open -> in_progress` edge.\n- Replacement walking retains outbound `duplicates` versus inbound `supersedes`, recorded/live liveness distinctions, administrative narrowing, fail-closed reads, unique conjunction matching, and mandatory-reason escape markers.\n- `tests/unit/test_close_disposition_attestation_738a.py` patches `_has_live_replacement_link` with `raising=False` and calls `find_replacement` positionally; the three seam names/signatures therefore remain explicit.\n- All four modules are collected directly by pytest. No `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, or pydoc consumer was found at the pinned base.\n\nPreserve this complete directive-bearing physical line byte-for-byte:\n\n```python\n    def _fail(*_a, **_k):  # pragma: no cover - reaching this IS the failure\n```\n\nAll other inline comments also remain unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Changes are limited to the 22 stable-ID prose blocks and adjacent blank lines; normalized-AST and token/comment comparisons pass for every owned path.\n- [x] Every edited block is shorter and preserves its listed constraint/consumer; historical narration, duplication, and separator ornament are removed.\n- [x] A reviewer who did not author the edits posts a leaf-linked TSV with one row per edited block: `stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session`.\n- [x] All 22 rows cite immutable blobs and record `directives_exact=PASS`, `semantic-preservation=PASS`, and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing/failing rows block closure.\n- [x] Focused pytest, scoped Ruff check/format, comment hygiene, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/unit/commands/test_close_disposition.py tests/unit/commands/test_compact_plan.py tests/unit/commands/test_lifecycle_cascade.py tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/ruff check tests/unit/commands/test_close_disposition.py tests/unit/commands/test_compact_plan.py tests/unit/commands/test_lifecycle_cascade.py tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/ruff format --check tests/unit/commands/test_close_disposition.py tests/unit/commands/test_compact_plan.py tests/unit/commands/test_lifecycle_cascade.py tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `git diff --check -- tests/unit/commands/test_close_disposition.py tests/unit/commands/test_compact_plan.py tests/unit/commands/test_lifecycle_cascade.py tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify`"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788770361195084894,"uuid":"baae9409-8b15-4d33-b6c5-60cc44c87bfb"}